1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,474
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:03,475 --> 00:00:10,000
It's a summary of N4 grammar!

3
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Interview Conversation / Japanese Interview Conversation

4
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,248
Excuse me, may I come in?

5
00:00:14,271 --> 00:00:17,104
Nice to meet you.

6
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:19,361
Nice to meet you.

7
00:00:19,384 --> 00:00:22,453
Please, have a seat.

8
00:00:22,476 --> 00:00:24,469
Okay.

9
00:00:24,492 --> 00:00:27,200
Thank you.

10
00:00:27,224 --> 00:00:30,924
This is an interview for a part-time job, right?

11
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:34,290
May I have your name, please?

12
00:00:34,314 --> 00:00:37,014
I'm Yamada.

13
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:39,903
Nice to meet you.

14
00:00:39,926 --> 00:00:43,760
Are you a student, Ms. Yamada?

15
00:00:43,783 --> 00:00:46,049
Okay.

16
00:00:46,072 --> 00:00:49,455
Yes, I'm a sophomore in university.

17
00:00:49,478 --> 00:00:51,978
I see.

18
00:00:52,001 --> 00:00:55,944
How's your Japanese study going?

19
00:00:55,967 --> 00:01:01,515
Kanji is tough, but conversation is fun.

20
00:01:01,539 --> 00:01:04,689
That's wonderful!

21
00:01:04,713 --> 00:01:09,547
What kind of work can you do, Ms. Yamada?

22
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:13,203
I can cook.

23
00:01:13,226 --> 00:01:16,403
And I can handle customer service too.

24
00:01:16,426 --> 00:01:19,406
You can cook, huh?

25
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:23,100
What kind of dishes can you make?

26
00:01:23,123 --> 00:01:27,304
I can make dishes like curry and hamburgers.

27
00:01:27,328 --> 00:01:29,697
That's great!

28
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:35,057
This shop gets really busy on weekends.

29
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:39,435
Can you work on Saturdays and Sundays?

30
00:01:39,458 --> 00:01:43,159
I can work on Saturdays.

31
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:47,299
Sundays are a bit difficult for me.

32
00:01:47,323 --> 00:01:49,489
Why is that?

33
00:01:49,512 --> 00:01:54,271
I have university classes on Sundays.

34
00:01:54,294 --> 00:01:56,794
I see.

35
00:01:56,817 --> 00:02:00,563
Working only on Saturdays is fine.

36
00:02:00,587 --> 00:02:02,853
Thank you.

37
00:02:02,876 --> 00:02:10,352
Ms. Yamada, you're cheerful, good at Japanese, and just perfect!

38
00:02:10,376 --> 00:02:13,143
Really?

39
00:02:13,166 --> 00:02:15,722
I'm so happy!

40
00:02:15,745 --> 00:02:20,245
We'd love to have you work at our shop!

41
00:02:20,268 --> 00:02:22,336
Okay.

42
00:02:22,359 --> 00:02:26,026
I'll do my best!

43
00:02:26,049 --> 00:02:31,207
The shop is close to the station, so it's convenient.

44
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:33,064
Okay.

45
00:02:33,087 --> 00:02:35,767
I know that well.

46
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:39,660
I'll give you the uniform tomorrow.

47
00:02:39,683 --> 00:02:42,117
Understood.

48
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:46,276
What time can you come tomorrow?

49
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:49,399
I can come at 3 PM.

50
00:02:49,422 --> 00:02:52,800
Great, we'll be waiting!

51
00:02:52,824 --> 00:02:54,758
Okay.

52
00:02:54,781 --> 00:02:57,881
Nice to meet you.

53
00:03:05,241 --> 00:03:06,741
Scene 2: Choosing and Trying on Clothes

54
00:03:06,741 --> 00:03:11,607
Excuse me, may I take a look around?

55
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:14,863
Yes, welcome!

56
00:03:14,886 --> 00:03:17,834
Please, go ahead and browse.

57
00:03:17,858 --> 00:03:23,091
This sweater looks really warm.

58
00:03:23,114 --> 00:03:28,951
Yes, that's our new winter sweater for this year.

59
00:03:28,975 --> 00:03:32,309
The colors are so beautiful.

60
00:03:32,332 --> 00:03:36,965
Yes, they're very popular.

61
00:03:36,988 --> 00:03:40,688
Can I try this on?

62
00:03:40,711 --> 00:03:43,744
Of course!

63
00:03:43,767 --> 00:03:46,700
The mirror is over there.

64
00:03:46,723 --> 00:03:49,062
Thank you.

65
00:03:49,086 --> 00:03:51,962
How does it look?

66
00:03:51,985 --> 00:03:54,656
Does it suit me?

67
00:03:54,679 --> 00:03:59,346
Yes, it looks great on you!

68
00:03:59,369 --> 00:04:03,469
But it seems a little big.

69
00:04:03,492 --> 00:04:06,128
I see.

70
00:04:06,151 --> 00:04:10,784
We have a smaller size too.

71
00:04:10,807 --> 00:04:15,241
I'll try the smaller size then.

72
00:04:15,264 --> 00:04:18,437
Please wait a moment.

73
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:21,206
Thank you for waiting.

74
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:23,930
Here you go.

75
00:04:23,953 --> 00:04:26,323
Thank you.

76
00:04:26,346 --> 00:04:30,500
Oh, this fits perfectly!

77
00:04:30,524 --> 00:04:33,862
It looks really warm.

78
00:04:33,885 --> 00:04:40,159
Yes, it's light and very comfortable to wear.

79
00:04:40,183 --> 00:04:43,533
Would you like to see other colors?

80
00:04:43,556 --> 00:04:47,232
What other colors do you have?

81
00:04:47,255 --> 00:04:50,769
We have red and blue.

82
00:04:50,793 --> 00:04:54,426
The blue sweater looks nice too.

83
00:04:54,449 --> 00:04:58,920
Yes, blue is popular as well.

84
00:04:58,944 --> 00:05:02,922
Hmm, I can't decide.

85
00:05:02,945 --> 00:05:06,245
Which one do you think is better?

86
00:05:06,268 --> 00:05:10,735
Do you wear a lot of white clothes?

87
00:05:10,758 --> 00:05:15,424
Yes, I wear white often.

88
00:05:15,447 --> 00:05:21,481
Then I think the blue sweater would suit you better.

89
00:05:21,504 --> 00:05:23,453
You're right.

90
00:05:23,477 --> 00:05:27,818
I'll take the blue sweater then.

91
00:05:27,841 --> 00:05:30,010
Thank you.

92
00:05:30,034 --> 00:05:32,967
Please proceed to the register.

93
00:05:32,990 --> 00:05:34,490
Scene 3: Discussing a Birthday Gift

94
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:39,557
Suzuki's birthday is coming up soon, isn't it?

95
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,365
You're right.

96
00:05:42,388 --> 00:05:46,066
It's next Friday.

97
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:50,190
Should we get her a gift?

98
00:05:50,213 --> 00:05:52,747
That's great!

99
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:56,203
What should we give her?

100
00:05:56,226 --> 00:06:00,659
What does Suzuki want?

101
00:06:00,682 --> 00:06:04,827
Hmm, I'm not sure.

102
00:06:04,851 --> 00:06:09,485
What did you give her last year?

103
00:06:09,508 --> 00:06:13,608
Last year, I gave her a book.

104
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:17,184
I gave her some sweets.

105
00:06:17,208 --> 00:06:23,647
How about we buy something together this year?

106
00:06:23,670 --> 00:06:28,104
Suzuki loves coffee, doesn't she?

107
00:06:28,127 --> 00:06:32,478
Yes, she drinks it every day.

108
00:06:32,501 --> 00:06:37,034
How about a coffee cup then?

109
00:06:37,057 --> 00:06:39,625
That's great!

110
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:43,558
Let's give her some coffee beans too.

111
00:06:43,581 --> 00:06:46,820
I think she'll be really happy.

112
00:06:46,843 --> 00:06:49,910
Where should we buy them?

113
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:54,599
There's a new shop in front of the station.

114
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:58,756
Let's go there tomorrow.

115
00:06:58,779 --> 00:07:04,316
By the way, Suzuki likes the color red, doesn't she?

116
00:07:04,339 --> 00:07:08,972
Yeah, I have a red car.

117
00:07:08,995 --> 00:07:13,303
Then let's look for a red cup.

118
00:07:13,326 --> 00:07:15,364
That's great!

119
00:07:15,388 --> 00:07:21,888
Oh, I’ll bake a cake for Suzuki-san next week too.

120
00:07:21,911 --> 00:07:25,177
That’s amazing!

121
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:28,267
I want to eat some too.

122
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:33,190
Then I’ll make one for your birthday too.

123
00:07:33,213 --> 00:07:35,756
Really?

124
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:38,685
I’m looking forward to it.

125
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:44,375
Let’s throw a party for Suzuki-san’s birthday with everyone!

126
00:07:44,398 --> 00:07:49,264
Sure, I’ll book a restaurant.

127
00:07:49,287 --> 00:07:52,042
Nice to meet you.

128
00:07:52,066 --> 00:07:56,299
It’s going to be a fun party!

129
00:07:56,322 --> 00:07:57,822
Scene 4: Trip Planning – Beach or Hot Spring?

130
00:07:57,822 --> 00:08:03,155
How about we all go on a trip this weekend?

131
00:08:03,178 --> 00:08:06,153
That's great!

132
00:08:06,177 --> 00:08:09,128
Where should we go?

133
00:08:09,152 --> 00:08:13,652
I’d love to go to the beach.

134
00:08:13,675 --> 00:08:16,309
The beach, huh?

135
00:08:16,332 --> 00:08:21,637
But it might rain this weekend.

136
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,693
What?

137
00:08:23,716 --> 00:08:26,216
Really?

138
00:08:26,239 --> 00:08:30,575
Yeah, the weather forecast said so.

139
00:08:30,599 --> 00:08:34,106
That’s too bad.

140
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:39,630
Since it might rain, how about going to a hot spring instead?

141
00:08:39,653 --> 00:08:44,847
A hot spring? That’s a great idea!

142
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:49,581
With a hot spring, we can still enjoy it even if it rains.

143
00:08:49,605 --> 00:08:53,723
Where should we go for the hot spring?

144
00:08:53,746 --> 00:08:56,459
How about Hakone?

145
00:08:56,482 --> 00:08:59,516
It’s close to Tokyo.

146
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:02,873
Hakone sounds great!

147
00:09:02,896 --> 00:09:06,597
I’d love to try some delicious food too.

148
00:09:06,621 --> 00:09:10,888
Shall we book a ryokan then?

149
00:09:10,911 --> 00:09:13,623
Yes, please.

150
00:09:13,646 --> 00:09:16,951
What kind of ryokan would you like?

151
00:09:16,975 --> 00:09:21,054
One with an open-air bath would be nice.

152
00:09:21,077 --> 00:09:25,510
Got it. I’ll look for one.

153
00:09:25,533 --> 00:09:28,900
Oh, are we going by car?

154
00:09:28,924 --> 00:09:31,624
Or by train?

155
00:09:31,647 --> 00:09:35,083
How about going by train?

156
00:09:35,106 --> 00:09:37,840
Why?

157
00:09:37,863 --> 00:09:42,696
The roads might be crowded this weekend.

158
00:09:42,719 --> 00:09:47,905
I see. With the train, we’ll know the exact time.

159
00:09:47,929 --> 00:09:52,595
Yeah. Let’s buy bento at the station and eat it.

160
00:09:52,618 --> 00:09:55,561
That sounds fun!

161
00:09:55,585 --> 00:09:59,343
Who else should we invite?

162
00:09:59,367 --> 00:10:03,201
How about inviting Tanaka-san too?

163
00:10:03,224 --> 00:10:06,357
That's great!

164
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:09,480
I’ll ask him tomorrow.

165
00:10:09,503 --> 00:10:12,736
Alright, thanks!

166
00:10:12,759 --> 00:10:16,693
Sure. I’ll get back to you soon.

167
00:10:16,717 --> 00:10:18,217
Scene 5: Preparing for the Barbecue

168
00:10:18,217 --> 00:10:22,883
I’m so excited for the barbecue next week!

169
00:10:22,906 --> 00:10:27,940
Yeah, I’m planning to eat a lot.

170
00:10:27,963 --> 00:10:31,429
How should we handle the preparations?

171
00:10:31,452 --> 00:10:35,961
I'll buy the meat.

172
00:10:35,984 --> 00:10:38,418
Thank you.

173
00:10:38,441 --> 00:10:44,022
I'm thinking of buying lots of beef and pork.

174
00:10:44,046 --> 00:10:47,781
Could you grab some chicken too?

175
00:10:47,804 --> 00:10:50,540
Got it.

176
00:10:50,564 --> 00:10:53,698
What about vegetables?

177
00:10:53,721 --> 00:10:58,072
I'll chop the veggies.

178
00:10:58,095 --> 00:11:00,664
That’d be a huge help!

179
00:11:00,687 --> 00:11:03,759
We’ll need drinks too.

180
00:11:03,783 --> 00:11:09,254
I’m planning to hit the supermarket tomorrow for groceries.

181
00:11:09,278 --> 00:11:14,178
It’s heavy, so I’ll come help you carry everything.

182
00:11:14,201 --> 00:11:16,377
Thank you.

183
00:11:16,401 --> 00:11:20,467
Let’s grab some beer and tea.

184
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:22,791
You're right.

185
00:11:22,814 --> 00:11:26,548
Do we have enough plates and cups?

186
00:11:26,570 --> 00:11:32,079
We’ve got them at home—I’ll bring them over.

187
00:11:32,103 --> 00:11:35,814
We should pick up some trash bags too.

188
00:11:35,837 --> 00:11:39,371
Okay, I’ll jot that down.

189
00:11:39,394 --> 00:11:43,227
What’s the weather looking like?

190
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:46,366
I think it’ll be sunny.

191
00:11:46,390 --> 00:11:50,057
What if it rains?

192
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:55,613
If it rains, let’s just have the party at my place.

193
00:11:55,636 --> 00:11:58,628
That sounds great too!

194
00:11:58,651 --> 00:12:02,584
Our friend Sato is coming too.

195
00:12:02,607 --> 00:12:07,480
Sato said he’ll bring his guitar.

196
00:12:07,504 --> 00:12:10,804
That’ll be so fun!

197
00:12:10,827 --> 00:12:14,728
I’ll bring my camera.

198
00:12:14,752 --> 00:12:18,542
Let’s take lots of photos!

199
00:12:18,565 --> 00:12:23,338
Yeah, I can’t wait for next week!

200
00:12:23,362 --> 00:12:25,995
Me neither!

201
00:12:26,018 --> 00:12:29,122
Let’s get everything ready!

202
00:12:29,145 --> 00:12:32,845
Will do—thanks for your help!

203
00:12:32,868 --> 00:12:34,368
Scene 6: Finding Your Perfect Rental – Must-Have Features

204
00:12:34,368 --> 00:12:39,606
Excuse me, I’m looking for an apartment.

205
00:12:39,629 --> 00:12:42,129
Welcome! How can I help?

206
00:12:42,152 --> 00:12:46,023
What kind of place are you looking for?

207
00:12:46,047 --> 00:12:51,880
I’d love a quiet place close to the station.

208
00:12:51,903 --> 00:12:56,536
How many minutes from the station would work for you?

209
00:12:56,559 --> 00:13:03,026
I’m looking for something within a 10-minute walk.

210
00:13:03,049 --> 00:13:05,919
Understood.

211
00:13:05,942 --> 00:13:10,076
What’s your budget for rent?

212
00:13:10,099 --> 00:13:14,289
Around 80,000 yen would be ideal.

213
00:13:14,312 --> 00:13:18,627
How about this place?

214
00:13:18,651 --> 00:13:23,584
Oh, I saw this one online yesterday!

215
00:13:23,607 --> 00:13:26,041
I see.

216
00:13:26,064 --> 00:13:30,964
It’s just a 5-minute walk from the station—super convenient!

217
00:13:30,987 --> 00:13:34,087
Is it spacious?

218
00:13:34,110 --> 00:13:36,508
Yes, it is.

219
00:13:36,531 --> 00:13:41,065
It’s bright with a south-facing window.

220
00:13:41,088 --> 00:13:43,754
That's great!

221
00:13:43,777 --> 00:13:47,244
Are pets allowed?

222
00:13:47,267 --> 00:13:50,059
I’m sorry.

223
00:13:50,083 --> 00:13:53,917
This place doesn’t allow pets.

224
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:56,895
I see.

225
00:13:56,918 --> 00:14:00,700
I have a cat.

226
00:14:00,724 --> 00:14:05,159
I need a place where I can live with my cat.

227
00:14:05,182 --> 00:14:08,249
Please wait a moment.

228
00:14:08,272 --> 00:14:10,544
I’d appreciate your help with that.

229
00:14:10,567 --> 00:14:13,901
How about this room?

230
00:14:13,924 --> 00:14:17,690
It looks a little old.

231
00:14:17,713 --> 00:14:19,947
Okay.

232
00:14:19,970 --> 00:14:24,603
But it's been newly renovated!

233
00:14:24,626 --> 00:14:28,693
Is there a supermarket nearby?

234
00:14:28,716 --> 00:14:30,982
Yes, it is.

235
00:14:31,005 --> 00:14:34,981
There's one just a three-minute walk away.

236
00:14:35,005 --> 00:14:38,838
That's really convenient!

237
00:14:38,861 --> 00:14:44,128
It's a quiet and safe neighborhood, so I highly recommend it.

238
00:14:44,151 --> 00:14:48,895
I'd love to see the room.

239
00:14:48,918 --> 00:14:51,357
Understood.

240
00:14:51,381 --> 00:14:54,557
Would you like to go check it out now?

241
00:14:54,581 --> 00:14:57,814
Yes, please.

242
00:14:57,837 --> 00:15:01,670
I'll drive you there.

243
00:15:01,693 --> 00:15:04,393
Right this way.

244
00:15:04,416 --> 00:15:06,398
Okay.

245
00:15:06,422 --> 00:15:09,055
Nice to meet you.

246
00:15:09,078 --> 00:15:12,664
Let me carry your luggage.

247
00:15:12,687 --> 00:15:16,060
Thank you.

248
00:15:16,084 --> 00:15:17,584
Scene 7: Moving In and Making Curry

249
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:23,936
Thanks so much for helping me move today.

250
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:28,226
Oh, it was nothing.

251
00:15:28,249 --> 00:15:34,431
I really appreciate you helping me with the heavy stuff.

252
00:15:34,455 --> 00:15:37,824
Don't mention it.

253
00:15:37,847 --> 00:15:41,354
We're getting hungry, aren't we?

254
00:15:41,378 --> 00:15:43,757
You're right.

255
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:47,325
Shall we grab something to eat?

256
00:15:47,349 --> 00:15:52,782
I'll make lunch for you.

257
00:15:52,805 --> 00:15:55,342
Really?

258
00:15:55,365 --> 00:15:58,199
I'm so happy!

259
00:15:58,222 --> 00:16:01,055
How about curry?

260
00:16:01,078 --> 00:16:05,815
Yes, I love curry!

261
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:10,379
Okay, just wait a little bit.

262
00:16:10,402 --> 00:16:12,318
Huh?

263
00:16:12,342 --> 00:16:15,212
What's wrong?

264
00:16:15,236 --> 00:16:19,988
Oh no, I dropped a plate.

265
00:16:20,011 --> 00:16:22,920
Are you okay?

266
00:16:22,944 --> 00:16:25,977
Did you get hurt?

267
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,633
Yes, I'm fine.

268
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:34,690
I'm so sorry I broke the plate.

269
00:16:34,713 --> 00:16:37,813
Don't mention it.

270
00:16:37,836 --> 00:16:41,408
I'll clean it up for you.

271
00:16:41,431 --> 00:16:45,982
Sorry about that, and thank you.

272
00:16:46,006 --> 00:16:50,872
Be careful not to cut yourself.

273
00:16:50,895 --> 00:16:54,162
I will, thanks.

274
00:16:54,185 --> 00:16:57,318
Where's the trash can?

275
00:16:57,341 --> 00:17:01,241
Just throw it in that box over there.

276
00:17:01,264 --> 00:17:03,964
Understood.

277
00:17:03,987 --> 00:17:07,157
I'm really sorry.

278
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:11,247
I'm just glad no one got hurt.

279
00:17:11,271 --> 00:17:16,038
You're so kind, thank you.

280
00:17:16,061 --> 00:17:19,370
Moving is tough, isn't it?

281
00:17:19,393 --> 00:17:26,583
Yeah, but I'm glad you helped me.

282
00:17:26,607 --> 00:17:30,707
If you need anything else, just call me.

283
00:17:30,730 --> 00:17:33,040
Thank you.

284
00:17:33,063 --> 00:17:36,203
The curry is ready!

285
00:17:36,227 --> 00:17:40,160
Wow, it looks delicious!

286
00:17:40,183 --> 00:17:43,283
Let's dig in!

287
00:17:43,306 --> 00:17:44,806
Scene 8: Procedures for Issuing Certificates

288
00:17:44,806 --> 00:17:47,309
I’m sorry.

289
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:50,599
Excuse me, may I have a moment?

290
00:17:50,622 --> 00:17:54,656
Yes, how can I help you?

291
00:17:54,679 --> 00:17:59,512
Could I get an academic transcript issued?

292
00:17:59,535 --> 00:18:02,168
Got it.

293
00:18:02,191 --> 00:18:05,870
May I see your student ID, please?

294
00:18:05,894 --> 00:18:09,164
Yes, this is it.

295
00:18:09,187 --> 00:18:11,520
Thank you.

296
00:18:11,543 --> 00:18:14,453
How many do you need?

297
00:18:14,477 --> 00:18:17,711
Two, please.

298
00:18:17,734 --> 00:18:20,167
Got it.

299
00:18:20,190 --> 00:18:25,029
Could you write your name on this paper, please?

300
00:18:25,052 --> 00:18:29,008
Sure, I'll write it here.

301
00:18:29,032 --> 00:18:32,544
Is this okay?

302
00:18:32,568 --> 00:18:35,526
Yes, that's fine.

303
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:40,668
Um, when can I get the certificate?

304
00:18:40,691 --> 00:18:43,885
It'll be ready by tomorrow afternoon.

305
00:18:43,909 --> 00:18:46,542
Tomorrow?

306
00:18:46,565 --> 00:18:51,913
Yes, the machine is broken today.

307
00:18:51,937 --> 00:18:56,709
I hope it's ready by tomorrow morning.

308
00:18:56,732 --> 00:18:59,365
Are you in a hurry?

309
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:05,055
Yes, I have a part-time job interview tomorrow.

310
00:19:05,078 --> 00:19:07,745
I see.

311
00:19:07,768 --> 00:19:12,203
In that case, I'll issue it this evening.

312
00:19:12,227 --> 00:19:14,893
Really?

313
00:19:14,916 --> 00:19:17,183
Thank you.

314
00:19:17,206 --> 00:19:20,673
Please come back around four.

315
00:19:20,696 --> 00:19:24,131
Okay, I'll be sure to come.

316
00:19:24,154 --> 00:19:27,987
Good luck with your interview!

317
00:19:28,010 --> 00:19:32,277
Yes, I hope I pass.

318
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:35,408
I'm sure you'll be fine.

319
00:19:35,431 --> 00:19:39,864
Thank you so much for your kindness.

320
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:44,398
You're welcome. Do you have any other questions?

321
00:19:44,422 --> 00:19:47,727
Yes, I'm fine.

322
00:19:47,751 --> 00:19:51,584
Then, I'll be expecting you at four.

323
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:54,240
Excuse me, may I come in?

324
00:19:54,263 --> 00:19:55,763
Scene 9: The Station-Front Bakery Closes and a New Building Rises

325
00:19:55,763 --> 00:20:02,030
I heard the bakery in front of the station is closing next month.

326
00:20:02,053 --> 00:20:05,953
What? Really?

327
00:20:05,976 --> 00:20:10,885
Yeah, Mr. Tanaka mentioned it.

328
00:20:10,908 --> 00:20:14,411
That’s too bad.

329
00:20:14,435 --> 00:20:19,004
But their bread was so good!

330
00:20:19,028 --> 00:20:23,340
It seems the owner got sick.

331
00:20:23,363 --> 00:20:26,297
Oh, I see.

332
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:29,455
That’s worrying.

333
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:35,411
They say a new building will go up next to the bakery.

334
00:20:35,434 --> 00:20:39,970
Oh? What kind of building?

335
00:20:39,994 --> 00:20:44,461
Looks like a big shopping mall.

336
00:20:44,484 --> 00:20:48,117
That’ll be convenient.

337
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:53,174
Yeah, I heard there’ll be a movie theater too.

338
00:20:53,197 --> 00:20:56,230
A movie theater?

339
00:20:56,253 --> 00:20:58,886
That's great!

340
00:20:58,909 --> 00:21:03,776
And a bunch of new clothing stores too, I hear.

341
00:21:03,799 --> 00:21:07,510
Shopping’s going to be fun!

342
00:21:07,534 --> 00:21:10,605
When will it open?

343
00:21:10,628 --> 00:21:14,544
They say it’ll be ready by next spring.

344
00:21:14,568 --> 00:21:17,936
I hope it’s soon!

345
00:21:17,959 --> 00:21:24,352
By the way, I heard Suzuki is getting married.

346
00:21:24,376 --> 00:21:28,109
What? To who?

347
00:21:28,132 --> 00:21:32,965
She said she’s marrying someone from work.

348
00:21:32,988 --> 00:21:36,266
That’s surprising!

349
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:41,057
They’re having the wedding next month, I think.

350
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:44,913
Do you think we’ll be invited?

351
00:21:44,936 --> 00:21:49,169
Hmm, I’m not sure.

352
00:21:49,192 --> 00:21:54,059
The wedding’s going to be in Hawaii, apparently.

353
00:21:54,082 --> 00:21:56,949
Hawaii, huh?

354
00:21:56,972 --> 00:21:59,672
That's great!

355
00:21:59,695 --> 00:22:04,395
I want to go to Hawaii too.

356
00:22:04,418 --> 00:22:07,384
It must be expensive, though.

357
00:22:07,407 --> 00:22:12,074
Yeah. I'll save up really hard.

358
00:22:12,097 --> 00:22:16,130
I think I'll start saving too.

359
00:22:16,153 --> 00:22:17,653
Scene 10: Introduction to Share House Rules

360
00:22:17,653 --> 00:22:21,720
Nice to meet you. Let's get along from today.

361
00:22:21,743 --> 00:22:24,720
Nice to meet you.

362
00:22:24,743 --> 00:22:29,656
Let me explain the share house rules.

363
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:32,676
Yes, please.

364
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:37,018
First, let's talk about how to take out the trash.

365
00:22:37,042 --> 00:22:41,108
Do we need to separate the trash?

366
00:22:41,131 --> 00:22:47,198
No, you must separate it before throwing it away.

367
00:22:47,221 --> 00:22:49,937
Understood.

368
00:22:49,961 --> 00:22:55,150
Burnable trash is collected on Mondays and Thursdays.

369
00:22:55,174 --> 00:22:58,713
When is non-burnable trash collected?

370
00:22:58,736 --> 00:23:03,508
Non-burnable trash is collected on Fridays.

371
00:23:03,532 --> 00:23:06,965
Got it. I'll remember that.

372
00:23:06,988 --> 00:23:11,422
Next, let's go over the bath rules.

373
00:23:11,445 --> 00:23:15,401
Can I take a bath anytime?

374
00:23:15,424 --> 00:23:21,137
Please don't take a bath after 10 PM.

375
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:23,669
Why is that?

376
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:30,126
It's noisy, so take a bath before others go to bed.

377
00:23:30,149 --> 00:23:32,663
Understood.

378
00:23:32,687 --> 00:23:35,285
I'll be careful.

379
00:23:35,309 --> 00:23:39,675
Now, about the washing machine.

380
00:23:39,698 --> 00:23:41,465
Okay.

381
00:23:41,488 --> 00:23:48,234
Check your pockets before using the washing machine.

382
00:23:48,257 --> 00:23:50,524
Understood.

383
00:23:50,547 --> 00:23:54,848
Don't do laundry late at night.

384
00:23:54,872 --> 00:23:57,871
Do it on the weekend instead.

385
00:23:57,894 --> 00:24:02,160
Okay, I'll do laundry on the weekend.

386
00:24:02,183 --> 00:24:06,518
Finally, the kitchen rules.

387
00:24:06,542 --> 00:24:10,175
Can I cook here?

388
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:13,103
Of course!

389
00:24:13,126 --> 00:24:19,193
Yes, but make sure to clean up after cooking.

390
00:24:19,216 --> 00:24:22,949
Sure, I'll keep it clean.

391
00:24:22,972 --> 00:24:26,956
That's all for the rules.

392
00:24:26,979 --> 00:24:31,246
Thank you for explaining everything so clearly.

393
00:24:31,269 --> 00:24:36,402
If you have any questions, feel free to ask anytime.

394
00:24:36,425 --> 00:24:40,732
Okay, thank you!

395
00:24:40,756 --> 00:24:42,256
Scene 11: Trouble with Forgotten Items

396
00:24:42,256 --> 00:24:45,404
What's wrong?

397
00:24:45,427 --> 00:24:48,403
You don't look so good.

398
00:24:48,427 --> 00:24:54,694
Actually, I left my bag on the train.

399
00:24:54,717 --> 00:24:58,877
Oh no! That's terrible.

400
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:04,470
I was so tired that I fell asleep on the train.

401
00:25:04,493 --> 00:25:08,264
You overslept, huh?

402
00:25:08,288 --> 00:25:14,254
Yeah, I rushed off when the train arrived at the station.

403
00:25:14,277 --> 00:25:17,711
What happened to your bag?

404
00:25:17,734 --> 00:25:22,000
I put it on the overhead rack.

405
00:25:22,023 --> 00:25:24,890
The overhead rack?

406
00:25:24,913 --> 00:25:32,060
Yeah, right after I got off, the doors closed.

407
00:25:32,083 --> 00:25:36,834
Oh, so your bag is still on the train.

408
00:25:36,858 --> 00:25:42,253
Yeah... I shouldn't have left it there.

409
00:25:42,277 --> 00:25:45,977
Did you tell the station staff?

410
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:50,792
Yes, I told them right away.

411
00:25:50,815 --> 00:25:54,328
Did they find your bag?

412
00:25:54,352 --> 00:25:57,585
Still haven't found it.

413
00:25:57,608 --> 00:26:01,841
What's in your bag?

414
00:26:01,864 --> 00:26:05,766
My wallet and keys are inside.

415
00:26:05,790 --> 00:26:10,372
That must be really tough.

416
00:26:10,396 --> 00:26:15,029
Yeah, I should've been more careful.

417
00:26:15,052 --> 00:26:17,519
You're right.

418
00:26:17,542 --> 00:26:23,493
I drank way too much last night.

419
00:26:23,516 --> 00:26:26,616
Did you overdo it?

420
00:26:26,639 --> 00:26:31,346
Yeah, that's why I couldn't wake up this morning.

421
00:26:31,369 --> 00:26:35,236
Did you almost miss your train?

422
00:26:35,259 --> 00:26:39,326
Yeah, I had to run to the station.

423
00:26:39,349 --> 00:26:43,386
You should've woken up earlier.

424
00:26:43,409 --> 00:26:46,942
I really think so too.

425
00:26:46,965 --> 00:26:51,632
Hope your bag turns up soon.

426
00:26:51,655 --> 00:26:54,763
Yes, thank you.

427
00:27:04,795 --> 00:27:06,295
Scene 12: Enjoy Making Curry Together

428
00:27:06,295 --> 00:27:10,995
Let's cook together now.

429
00:27:11,018 --> 00:27:15,167
Sure! What are we making?

430
00:27:15,190 --> 00:27:19,379
We're making curry today.

431
00:27:19,402 --> 00:27:21,988
That's great!

432
00:27:22,011 --> 00:27:26,164
What can I help with?

433
00:27:26,187 --> 00:27:30,254
How about chopping the vegetables?

434
00:27:30,277 --> 00:27:32,860
Understood.

435
00:27:32,883 --> 00:27:36,717
Carrots and onions, right?

436
00:27:36,740 --> 00:27:41,573
Yes, and I'll sauté the meat.

437
00:27:41,596 --> 00:27:45,696
Want to cook while listening to some music?

438
00:27:45,719 --> 00:27:48,619
That's great!

439
00:27:48,642 --> 00:27:51,942
Go ahead and play your favorite.

440
00:27:51,965 --> 00:27:55,665
I'll put on some jazz.

441
00:27:55,688 --> 00:28:00,488
Cooking with music is so much fun!

442
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:04,945
Okay, I've finished chopping the veggies.

443
00:28:04,968 --> 00:28:07,540
Thank you.

444
00:28:07,564 --> 00:28:10,754
Add them to the pot.

445
00:28:10,777 --> 00:28:14,644
Got it, putting them in now.

446
00:28:14,667 --> 00:28:18,819
Next, add water and let it simmer.

447
00:28:18,843 --> 00:28:21,709
How long should we simmer it?

448
00:28:21,732 --> 00:28:24,966
About twenty minutes.

449
00:28:24,989 --> 00:28:27,222
Understood.

450
00:28:27,245 --> 00:28:32,547
This will make it instantly delicious!

451
00:28:32,570 --> 00:28:35,239
What is it?

452
00:28:35,263 --> 00:28:38,059
Chocolate.

453
00:28:38,082 --> 00:28:43,798
Wait, you put chocolate in curry?!

454
00:28:43,821 --> 00:28:50,354
Yes! Chocolate makes the flavor smoother.

455
00:28:50,377 --> 00:28:54,044
Wow, I had no idea.

456
00:28:54,067 --> 00:28:57,256
You should try it sometime.

457
00:28:57,279 --> 00:29:02,795
Okay, I'll add it next time I make curry.

458
00:29:02,819 --> 00:29:06,174
It smells amazing already!

459
00:29:06,197 --> 00:29:11,464
It really does—I'm getting hungry!

460
00:29:11,487 --> 00:29:14,587
Almost done!

461
00:29:14,610 --> 00:29:17,727
I can't wait to eat!

462
00:29:17,751 --> 00:29:19,251
Scene 13: Hotel Check-in Procedure

463
00:29:19,251 --> 00:29:24,084
Excuse me, I'd like to check in.

464
00:29:24,107 --> 00:29:26,622
Welcome! How can I help?

465
00:29:26,646 --> 00:29:30,579
May I have your name, please?

466
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:32,983
Tanaka.

467
00:29:33,007 --> 00:29:35,707
Mr./Ms. Tanaka, correct?

468
00:29:35,730 --> 00:29:38,830
We've been expecting you.

469
00:29:38,853 --> 00:29:42,237
I made a reservation online.

470
00:29:42,260 --> 00:29:44,896
Understood.

471
00:29:44,919 --> 00:29:47,753
Let me confirm that for you.

472
00:29:47,776 --> 00:29:50,809
I apologize for the inconvenience.

473
00:29:50,832 --> 00:29:55,165
We can't seem to find Mr. Tanaka's reservation.

474
00:29:55,188 --> 00:30:01,455
What? I definitely booked it a month ago!

475
00:30:01,478 --> 00:30:05,028
When did you make the reservation?

476
00:30:05,051 --> 00:30:08,626
October 5th.

477
00:30:08,650 --> 00:30:12,521
I should have also received a confirmation email.

478
00:30:12,544 --> 00:30:15,740
Let me check again.

479
00:30:15,764 --> 00:30:18,997
Please wait a moment.

480
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:21,654
Yes, please.

481
00:30:21,677 --> 00:30:24,543
Thank you for waiting.

482
00:30:24,566 --> 00:30:29,338
We’ve confirmed Mr. Tanaka’s reservation.

483
00:30:29,361 --> 00:30:32,634
Oh, that’s a relief!

484
00:30:32,658 --> 00:30:36,604
We sincerely apologize for the trouble.

485
00:30:36,628 --> 00:30:39,961
No worries. It’s fine.

486
00:30:39,984 --> 00:30:45,217
Today, we’ve prepared a room with an ocean view for you.

487
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:48,107
That’s wonderful!

488
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:51,845
Let me carry your luggage for you.

489
00:30:51,868 --> 00:30:54,172
Thank you.

490
00:30:54,196 --> 00:30:57,862
Your room is on the 10th floor.

491
00:30:57,885 --> 00:31:00,952
Which floor is the restaurant on?

492
00:31:00,975 --> 00:31:04,692
The restaurant is on the first floor.

493
00:31:04,715 --> 00:31:08,382
What time is breakfast served?

494
00:31:08,405 --> 00:31:13,772
Breakfast is available from 7:00 AM to 10:00 AM.

495
00:31:13,795 --> 00:31:16,070
Understood.

496
00:31:16,094 --> 00:31:21,327
We also have a large public bath—please feel free to use it.

497
00:31:21,350 --> 00:31:24,683
Sure, I’ll check it out.

498
00:31:24,706 --> 00:31:28,810
Now, let me show you to your room.

499
00:31:28,834 --> 00:31:31,867
Nice to meet you.

500
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,390
Scene 14: Gratitude and Farewell

501
00:31:33,390 --> 00:31:38,957
Senior, it’s going to feel lonely without you starting tomorrow.

502
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:41,178
Yeah, it really has been.

503
00:31:41,202 --> 00:31:46,268
Three years just flew by.

504
00:31:46,291 --> 00:31:51,807
Thank you so much for everything you’ve taught me.

505
00:31:51,831 --> 00:31:56,210
Oh, no—I should be thanking *you*.

506
00:31:56,234 --> 00:32:02,175
I really appreciated how you always helped me when I messed up.

507
00:32:02,198 --> 00:32:06,465
Everyone makes mistakes at first.

508
00:32:06,488 --> 00:32:11,389
Thanks to you, work became so much more enjoyable.

509
00:32:11,412 --> 00:32:16,482
I’m really happy to hear that.

510
00:32:16,506 --> 00:32:20,025
Good luck at your new company!

511
00:32:20,049 --> 00:32:22,183
Thanks.

512
00:32:22,206 --> 00:32:25,439
I’m a little nervous, though.

513
00:32:25,462 --> 00:32:29,605
You’ll do great—no doubt about it.

514
00:32:29,628 --> 00:32:33,007
You keep up the good work too.

515
00:32:33,030 --> 00:32:34,811
Okay.

516
00:32:34,835 --> 00:32:37,935
I'll do my best!

517
00:32:37,958 --> 00:32:42,912
If you ever have questions, don’t hesitate to reach out anytime.

518
00:32:42,936 --> 00:32:45,302
Thank you.

519
00:32:45,325 --> 00:32:47,693
I will.

520
00:32:47,717 --> 00:32:51,217
Don’t overwork yourself, okay?

521
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:53,140
Okay.

522
00:32:53,162 --> 00:32:55,629
I'll be careful.

523
00:32:55,652 --> 00:32:59,359
Make sure to take breaks once in a while.

524
00:32:59,383 --> 00:33:01,686
Okay.

525
00:33:01,709 --> 00:33:06,243
I’m sure the new environment will be tiring for you too.

526
00:33:06,266 --> 00:33:08,732
Yeah, it really has been.

527
00:33:08,755 --> 00:33:13,259
Please take care of yourself in your new chapter.

528
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:15,656
Thanks.

529
00:33:15,679 --> 00:33:18,668
Health comes first, after all.

530
00:33:18,691 --> 00:33:22,890
Let’s all go out for a meal together again soon!

531
00:33:22,913 --> 00:33:25,384
Of course!

532
00:33:25,407 --> 00:33:27,347
Please invite me.

533
00:33:27,371 --> 00:33:29,325
Okay.

534
00:33:29,349 --> 00:33:31,894
I definitely will.

535
00:33:31,917 --> 00:33:34,617
See you later.

536
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,718
Okay.

537
00:33:36,742 --> 00:33:40,339
Thank you so much for everything up until now.

538
00:33:40,362 --> 00:33:44,262
No, thank *you* so much.

539
00:33:44,285 --> 00:33:46,619
Take care.

540
00:33:46,642 --> 00:33:50,542
You too. Goodbye.

541
00:33:50,565 --> 00:33:52,065
Scene 15: Farewells and First Conversations / Basic Greetings and Initial Conversations

542
00:33:52,065 --> 00:33:54,798
Excuse me.

543
00:33:54,821 --> 00:33:57,321
We've been expecting you.

544
00:33:57,344 --> 00:34:00,343
Please, come in.

545
00:34:00,366 --> 00:34:04,738
Thank you for taking time out of your busy schedule today.

546
00:34:04,762 --> 00:34:10,200
Not at all, thank *you* for coming all this way.

547
00:34:10,223 --> 00:34:15,557
I’m Yamada from Mirai Corporation.

548
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:19,246
Nice to meet you. I’m Sato.

549
00:34:19,269 --> 00:34:22,502
Thank you for your continued support.

550
00:34:22,525 --> 00:34:26,279
No, thank *you* for your support.

551
00:34:26,303 --> 00:34:28,858
Please, have a seat.

552
00:34:28,881 --> 00:34:31,514
Excuse me.

553
00:34:31,537 --> 00:34:35,104
Did you come by train today?

554
00:34:35,127 --> 00:34:39,366
Yes, I took the Shinkansen.

555
00:34:39,389 --> 00:34:42,975
I see. That must have been a long trip.

556
00:34:42,999 --> 00:34:46,981
No, it only took about two hours.

557
00:34:47,004 --> 00:34:49,904
That’s great to hear.

558
00:34:49,927 --> 00:34:54,723
This is just a little something, but please accept it.

559
00:34:54,747 --> 00:34:58,327
Thank you so much for your thoughtfulness.

560
00:34:58,350 --> 00:35:01,088
What is this?

561
00:35:01,112 --> 00:35:05,012
It’s a snack called Tokyo Banana.

562
00:35:05,035 --> 00:35:08,735
Oh, I’ve heard of it!

563
00:35:08,758 --> 00:35:11,664
It’s a famous snack, isn’t it?

564
00:35:11,687 --> 00:35:16,154
Yes, it’s very popular in Tokyo.

565
00:35:16,177 --> 00:35:19,244
We’ll share it with everyone in the office.

566
00:35:19,267 --> 00:35:23,237
Please, enjoy it with your team.

567
00:35:23,261 --> 00:35:25,627
Thank you.

568
00:35:25,650 --> 00:35:31,205
Now, let me explain our new product.

569
00:35:31,229 --> 00:35:34,381
Yes, please go ahead.

570
00:35:34,404 --> 00:35:38,598
Could you take a look at this document?

571
00:35:38,622 --> 00:35:41,924
Yes, I’ll take a look.

572
00:35:41,948 --> 00:35:46,720
This product is very user-friendly.

573
00:35:46,743 --> 00:35:51,057
I see. The design is great too.

574
00:35:51,081 --> 00:35:53,314
Thank you.

575
00:35:53,337 --> 00:35:57,171
Let me think about it for a bit.

576
00:35:57,194 --> 00:35:58,694
Scene 16: Key Points in Choosing a Smartphone / Smartphone Selection Tips

577
00:35:58,694 --> 00:36:03,994
I’m thinking of buying a new smartphone.

578
00:36:04,017 --> 00:36:06,683
That's great!

579
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:10,615
What kind of smartphone should I get?

580
00:36:10,639 --> 00:36:16,672
I’m concerned about whether the camera takes good photos.

581
00:36:16,695 --> 00:36:22,528
Most recent smartphones have great cameras.

582
00:36:22,551 --> 00:36:25,330
I see.

583
00:36:25,354 --> 00:36:29,520
What size do you think is best?

584
00:36:29,543 --> 00:36:34,810
I don’t like screens that are too small and hard to see.

585
00:36:34,833 --> 00:36:38,867
Then a larger screen would be better, right?

586
00:36:38,890 --> 00:36:44,063
But if it’s too big, it’s hard to hold.

587
00:36:44,087 --> 00:36:46,856
That’s true.

588
00:36:46,879 --> 00:36:52,346
It’s best to go to a store and try holding one in person.

589
00:36:52,369 --> 00:36:54,524
You're right.

590
00:36:54,547 --> 00:36:58,614
Because you can tell if it's heavy or not.

591
00:36:58,637 --> 00:37:02,470
What do you think of this model?

592
00:37:02,493 --> 00:37:06,599
It's very popular.

593
00:37:06,623 --> 00:37:10,257
Is it easy to use?

594
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:14,513
Yes, it's very user-friendly.

595
00:37:14,536 --> 00:37:19,403
Ease of use for beginners is really important.

596
00:37:19,425 --> 00:37:24,601
Then this is the one I'd recommend the most.

597
00:37:24,624 --> 00:37:28,258
Does the battery last long?

598
00:37:28,281 --> 00:37:33,714
Yes, you can use it all day without any issues.

599
00:37:33,737 --> 00:37:37,697
I also want to know if it's durable.

600
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:42,387
It uses shatter-resistant glass, so it won’t break easily even if dropped.

601
00:37:42,410 --> 00:37:45,643
That’s reassuring.

602
00:37:45,666 --> 00:37:48,974
Which color do you prefer?

603
00:37:48,998 --> 00:37:52,831
I'm torn between white and black.

604
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:57,042
I think black looks cooler.

605
00:37:57,066 --> 00:38:00,133
Then I’ll go with black.

606
00:38:00,156 --> 00:38:04,989
You should get a case too.

607
00:38:05,012 --> 00:38:06,979
You're right.

608
00:38:07,002 --> 00:38:11,198
I’ll look for a scratch-resistant one.

609
00:38:11,221 --> 00:38:16,121
Want me to come with you when you go buy it?

610
00:38:16,144 --> 00:38:19,811
Yes, I’d appreciate that.

611
00:38:19,834 --> 00:38:21,334
Scene 17: Troubles in a Crowded Train

612
00:38:21,334 --> 00:38:24,171
Good morning.

613
00:38:24,194 --> 00:38:27,027
Good morning.

614
00:38:27,050 --> 00:38:31,317
You look really tired.

615
00:38:31,340 --> 00:38:38,112
Yeah, my morning commute was rough.

616
00:38:38,135 --> 00:38:40,925
Was it a packed train?

617
00:38:40,949 --> 00:38:46,027
Yes, it was even more crowded than usual.

618
00:38:46,051 --> 00:38:49,351
That sounds awful.

619
00:38:49,374 --> 00:38:55,253
Someone stepped on my foot while I was on the train.

620
00:38:55,276 --> 00:38:59,258
Ouch! That must’ve hurt.

621
00:38:59,281 --> 00:39:03,453
It did. It hurt a lot.

622
00:39:03,476 --> 00:39:06,776
Did they apologize?

623
00:39:06,799 --> 00:39:13,699
No, it was so crowded I couldn’t tell who did it.

624
00:39:13,722 --> 00:39:17,556
That’s just bad luck.

625
00:39:17,578 --> 00:39:20,770
And that’s not all.

626
00:39:20,794 --> 00:39:24,227
There’s more?

627
00:39:24,250 --> 00:39:29,725
My bag got stuck in the door when it closed.

628
00:39:29,749 --> 00:39:32,529
Your bag did?

629
00:39:32,552 --> 00:39:35,385
Was it okay?

630
00:39:35,408 --> 00:39:41,247
I was so embarrassed until we reached the next station.

631
00:39:41,271 --> 00:39:45,004
Everyone was staring, right?

632
00:39:45,027 --> 00:39:50,260
Yeah, it was the worst morning ever.

633
00:39:50,283 --> 00:39:57,183
I once had my wallet stolen on a crowded train too.

634
00:39:57,206 --> 00:40:01,782
Wait, your wallet was stolen?

635
00:40:01,805 --> 00:40:06,839
Yeah, while I was asleep.

636
00:40:06,862 --> 00:40:09,772
That’s terrifying.

637
00:40:09,795 --> 00:40:14,895
You really need to be careful on packed trains.

638
00:40:14,918 --> 00:40:20,052
I’ll make sure to hold my bag tightly from now on.

639
00:40:20,075 --> 00:40:24,641
Leaving a little earlier to avoid the rush might help too.

640
00:40:24,664 --> 00:40:26,939
You're right.

641
00:40:26,963 --> 00:40:31,429
I’ll leave home a bit earlier starting tomorrow.

642
00:40:31,452 --> 00:40:34,352
That’s a good idea.

643
00:40:34,375 --> 00:40:39,052
I just want to go home early and rest today.

644
00:40:39,076 --> 00:40:41,743
Please do.

645
00:40:41,766 --> 00:40:44,666
You must be tired. Take care.

646
00:40:44,689 --> 00:40:46,189
Scene 18: Party Prep – Let’s Get Decorating!

647
00:40:46,189 --> 00:40:50,656
The party’s finally tomorrow!

648
00:40:50,679 --> 00:40:53,146
You're right.

649
00:40:53,169 --> 00:40:56,160
I can’t wait!

650
00:40:56,183 --> 00:41:00,250
Let’s decorate the room.

651
00:41:00,273 --> 00:41:02,106
Okay.

652
00:41:02,129 --> 00:41:05,762
Where should we start?

653
00:41:05,785 --> 00:41:10,652
There are flowers on the table already.

654
00:41:10,675 --> 00:41:12,508
Yes, it is.

655
00:41:12,531 --> 00:41:15,705
I bought them yesterday.

656
00:41:15,728 --> 00:41:19,109
They’re so pretty!

657
00:41:19,133 --> 00:41:21,407
Thank you.

658
00:41:21,430 --> 00:41:26,349
I want the room to feel brighter.

659
00:41:26,373 --> 00:41:28,746
Understood.

660
00:41:28,770 --> 00:41:32,109
I’ll turn on all the lights.

661
00:41:32,133 --> 00:41:36,833
Let’s hang some balloons on the walls.

662
00:41:36,856 --> 00:41:39,813
What kind of balloons do you want?

663
00:41:39,836 --> 00:41:44,569
I’d love some colorful ones.

664
00:41:44,592 --> 00:41:51,026
Okay, I’ll blow up red, blue, and yellow balloons.

665
00:41:51,049 --> 00:41:53,515
I’d appreciate your help with that.

666
00:41:53,538 --> 00:41:57,905
I’ll put up some pictures on the walls.

667
00:41:57,929 --> 00:42:01,429
There are posters up already, too.

668
00:42:01,452 --> 00:42:04,038
Me neither!

669
00:42:04,061 --> 00:42:06,801
This is looking great!

670
00:42:06,825 --> 00:42:10,292
What about music?

671
00:42:10,315 --> 00:42:14,252
Let’s play something fun!

672
00:42:14,275 --> 00:42:19,024
Okay, I’ll put on this CD.

673
00:42:19,048 --> 00:42:22,414
How’s the volume?

674
00:42:22,437 --> 00:42:27,504
Should I turn it up a little?

675
00:42:27,527 --> 00:42:34,304
No, it’ll drown out our voices. Let’s keep it a bit lower.

676
00:42:34,328 --> 00:42:36,961
Understood.

677
00:42:36,984 --> 00:42:40,094
I’ll turn it down.

678
00:42:40,117 --> 00:42:44,251
Are the drinks chilled?

679
00:42:44,274 --> 00:42:46,574
Okay.

680
00:42:46,597 --> 00:42:49,663
They’re in the fridge.

681
00:42:49,686 --> 00:42:53,960
Are the plates and cups set out?

682
00:42:53,983 --> 00:42:58,933
Yep, they’re all lined up on the shelf.

683
00:42:58,957 --> 00:43:02,457
Everything’s ready to go!

684
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:04,780
Okay.

685
00:43:04,803 --> 00:43:08,574
Tomorrow’s gonna be so much fun!

686
00:43:08,597 --> 00:43:10,097
Scene 19: Test Scores – Time for Some Reflection

687
00:43:10,097 --> 00:43:13,997
Takashi, come here for a second.

688
00:43:14,020 --> 00:43:16,854
What is it, Mom?

689
00:43:16,877 --> 00:43:21,224
Show me your quiz results from today.

690
00:43:21,247 --> 00:43:25,281
Ugh, I’ll show you later.

691
00:43:25,304 --> 00:43:28,692
Show me now.

692
00:43:28,715 --> 00:43:31,981
Fine, here.

693
00:43:32,004 --> 00:43:35,717
What is this? A 30?

694
00:43:35,741 --> 00:43:38,913
It’s just 30 points.

695
00:43:38,936 --> 00:43:43,236
But it was so hard!

696
00:43:43,259 --> 00:43:47,596
This is what happens when you don’t study every day.

697
00:43:47,620 --> 00:43:50,795
I’ll do better starting tomorrow.

698
00:43:50,819 --> 00:43:54,556
You say that every day.

699
00:43:54,579 --> 00:43:59,526
I promised my friends I’d hang out with them today.

700
00:43:59,549 --> 00:44:02,856
You’re not going anywhere.

701
00:44:02,880 --> 00:44:06,276
What? Why not?

702
00:44:06,299 --> 00:44:10,937
Finish your homework first, then you can go.

703
00:44:10,960 --> 00:44:14,394
I'll do it when I get back.

704
00:44:14,417 --> 00:44:16,373
No way.

705
00:44:16,397 --> 00:44:19,897
Do your homework right now.

706
00:44:19,920 --> 00:44:22,787
Alright.

707
00:44:22,810 --> 00:44:27,076
You really need to study more.

708
00:44:27,099 --> 00:44:30,966
Don't make me study all the time!

709
00:44:30,989 --> 00:44:36,022
If you get good grades, I'll buy you a game.

710
00:44:36,045 --> 00:44:38,356
Really?

711
00:44:38,380 --> 00:44:41,513
You promise, right?

712
00:44:41,536 --> 00:44:47,503
Yes. If you score over 80 on your next test.

713
00:44:47,526 --> 00:44:50,668
Alright, I'll do my best!

714
00:44:50,691 --> 00:44:55,993
But first, clean up your room.

715
00:44:56,017 --> 00:45:00,283
Ugh, do I have to clean my room too?

716
00:45:00,306 --> 00:45:03,015
Of course.

717
00:45:03,039 --> 00:45:07,391
You can't focus if your room is messy.

718
00:45:07,414 --> 00:45:11,548
Fine, I'll clean it right away.

719
00:45:11,571 --> 00:45:14,726
Call me when you're done.

720
00:45:14,749 --> 00:45:17,383
Okaaay!

721
00:45:17,406 --> 00:45:18,906
Scene 20: The Daily Grind of Overtime Hell

722
00:45:18,906 --> 00:45:23,063
Man, I'm exhausted today.

723
00:45:23,086 --> 00:45:25,860
Me neither!

724
00:45:25,883 --> 00:45:30,117
Lately, it's nothing but overtime.

725
00:45:30,140 --> 00:45:34,077
What time did you get home yesterday?

726
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:37,576
Eleven at night.

727
00:45:37,600 --> 00:45:41,953
The boss made me work late.

728
00:45:41,976 --> 00:45:45,730
That sounds awful.

729
00:45:45,753 --> 00:45:50,656
I had to redo all the documents.

730
00:45:50,679 --> 00:45:54,394
Wait, *all* of them?

731
00:45:54,418 --> 00:45:59,085
Yeah, I'm so done with this.

732
00:45:59,108 --> 00:46:06,014
Working like this every day is killing me.

733
00:46:06,037 --> 00:46:11,072
Tell me about it. No matter how much I sleep, I'm still tired.

734
00:46:11,095 --> 00:46:14,329
Are you working this weekend too?

735
00:46:14,352 --> 00:46:19,018
They're making me come in on Sunday.

736
00:46:19,041 --> 00:46:22,584
That's no break at all!

737
00:46:22,607 --> 00:46:25,274
Exactly.

738
00:46:25,297 --> 00:46:28,730
I just want to rest properly.

739
00:46:28,753 --> 00:46:34,312
Even if we complain to the boss, nothing changes.

740
00:46:34,336 --> 00:46:38,769
Yeah, I think it's pointless no matter what we say.

741
00:46:38,792 --> 00:46:45,826
Lately, I've been swamped with new work too.

742
00:46:45,850 --> 00:46:48,528
We're both in the same boat, huh?

743
00:46:48,551 --> 00:46:53,733
Next month, I'm leaving on time.

744
00:46:53,757 --> 00:46:57,590
Wait, you can actually leave on time?

745
00:46:57,613 --> 00:47:04,164
Yep. No matter how busy, I'm prioritizing my time.

746
00:47:04,188 --> 00:47:07,621
That's a great mindset.

747
00:47:07,644 --> 00:47:12,439
I'm sick of a life that's just work, work, work.

748
00:47:12,463 --> 00:47:17,797
From now on, I'm going to start saying no to work.

749
00:47:17,820 --> 00:47:23,486
That's right. If it's too much, just say no.

750
00:47:23,509 --> 00:47:28,818
Yeah, my health comes first.

751
00:47:28,842 --> 00:47:33,175
Well then, should we head home for today?

752
00:47:33,198 --> 00:47:38,376
Yeah, let's call it a day and go home early.

753
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:40,916
You must be tired. Take care.

754
00:47:40,940 --> 00:47:43,933
You must be tired. Take care.